WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.523 --> 00:00:13.444
have to get to Mrs.

2
00:00:13.564 --> 00:00:15.385
Bun's house," Roxy thought.

3
00:00:16.046 --> 00:00:17.447
"Someone robbed her guests!"

4
00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:21.109
"I'll be right back!

5
00:00:21.669 --> 00:00:22.870
I need to call my parents."

6
00:00:23.411 --> 00:00:24.632
Roxy yelled to her friends.

7
00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:28.634
"Don't take too long," Terrell said.

8
00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:30.936
"The concert is starting soon."

9
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.461
A moment later Roxy shot up into the sky.

10
00:00:34.481 --> 00:00:37.983
"Whoa!" Mara cried.

11
00:00:38.003 --> 00:00:39.784
"Rocket Girl!"

12
00:00:42.065 --> 00:00:43.126
Roxy arrived at Mrs.

13
00:00:43.186 --> 00:00:43.766
Bun's house.

14
00:00:45.787 --> 00:00:49.590
Mrs. Bun looked upset as Detective Smith crawled around in some rosebushes.

15
00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:51.791
Roxy grinned.

16
00:00:51.811 --> 00:00:54.692
"Doing some gardening, Detective?"

17
00:00:58.434 --> 00:00:59.315
Rocket Girl."

18
00:00:59.695 --> 00:01:01.236
Detective Smith pretended to laugh.

19
00:01:02.764 --> 00:01:05.065
"I—ouch! A thorn poked me."

20
00:01:06.386 --> 00:01:08.467
He got back to his feet and held up his notebook.

21
00:01:08.487 --> 00:01:11.489
"I dropped this in the rosebushes."

22
00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:13.650
The detective turned to Mrs.

23
00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.391
Bun. "I'm sorry.

24
00:01:15.411 --> 00:01:16.051
What were you saying?"

25
00:01:17.152 --> 00:01:18.693
Mrs. Bun took a deep breath.

26
00:01:18.713 --> 00:01:22.175
"I was telling you about my guests.

27
00:01:22.655 --> 00:01:25.516
They are all still here if you want to talk to them.

28
00:01:25.836 --> 00:01:28.318
The servers and the quartet are here too."

29
00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:32.180
"Quartet?" Detective Smith raised an eyebrow.

30
00:01:33.512 --> 00:01:35.894
"A string quartet," Mrs.

31
00:01:35.974 --> 00:01:36.555
Bun said.

32
00:01:36.575 --> 00:01:40.659
"I hired four musicians to play during the party."

33
00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:43.401
"What happened before the robbery?"

34
00:01:43.641 --> 00:01:44.302
Roxy asked.

35
00:01:44.322 --> 00:01:47.385
"Did you see anything suspicious?"

36
00:01:48.846 --> 00:01:49.827
Mrs. Bun shrugged.

37
00:01:49.847 --> 00:01:54.031
"It's odd, but I don't remember anything.

38
00:01:54.772 --> 00:01:57.834
One minute we were enjoying a lovely afternoon.

39
00:01:58.175 --> 00:02:01.581
And the next minute, everyone's wallets were missing!

40
00:02:02.041 --> 00:02:03.602
Our jewelry too!"

41
00:02:04.963 --> 00:02:06.464
Detective Smith made some notes.

42
00:02:06.484 --> 00:02:09.846
"We'll need to interview everyone, Mrs.

43
00:02:09.966 --> 00:02:13.167
Bun." Roxy spotted the musicians.

44
00:02:14.908 --> 00:02:16.029
"Let's start with them."

45
00:02:21.672 --> 00:02:23.673
anybody see anything suspicious?"

46
00:02:24.153 --> 00:02:25.314
Roxy asked the musicians.

47
00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:28.636
"No," the cellist said.

48
00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:30.761
"But I hope you find the criminal.

49
00:02:31.381 --> 00:02:33.122
That thief stole my new watch."

50
00:02:34.223 --> 00:02:35.784
He looked at his cello and sighed.

51
00:02:36.924 --> 00:02:38.605
"I'm just glad I still have this."

52
00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:42.487
"My ruby earrings are gone!"

53
00:02:42.988 --> 00:02:43.908
a violinist said.

54
00:02:43.928 --> 00:02:47.890
"Wait a second," Detective Smith said.

55
00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.572
"There are only three of you.

56
00:02:51.772 --> 00:02:53.773
Mrs. Bun said you were a quartet."

57
00:02:53.793 --> 00:02:56.795
"Oh, goodness!"

58
00:02:57.255 --> 00:02:58.336
the third musician said.

59
00:02:59.348 --> 00:03:00.369
"Where's Violet?"

60
00:03:00.389 --> 00:03:03.250
"Who?" Roxy asked.

61
00:03:04.191 --> 00:03:06.312
"Violet Sharp," the cellist said.

62
00:03:06.332 --> 00:03:08.694
"She's our other violinist."

63
00:03:08.714 --> 00:03:11.815
"Hmm," Roxy said.

64
00:03:11.835 --> 00:03:15.558
"Someone robbed the guests, and now Violet is gone.

65
00:03:16.318 --> 00:03:18.019
That's pretty suspicious."

66
00:03:18.039 --> 00:03:21.681
"Nonsense," the violinist said.

67
00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.662
"Violet is no thief.

68
00:03:24.083 --> 00:03:26.264
She's a very talented musician.

69
00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.582
In fact, the Metro City Symphony Orchestra invited her to try out."

70
00:03:32.803 --> 00:03:35.064
"Impressive," Detective Smith said.

71
00:03:35.765 --> 00:03:36.805
Then his phone beeped.

72
00:03:36.825 --> 00:03:41.107
"Hello? Oh no!

73
00:03:41.527 --> 00:03:42.408
We'll be right there!"

74
00:03:43.929 --> 00:03:45.329
He hung up and looked at Roxy.

75
00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:47.891
"Another robbery just took place.

76
00:03:48.231 --> 00:03:50.352
This one was at Metro City Shopping Mall!"
